      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "HUANG Fang-tu 黃芳度 (T. 壽巖), d. Nov. 22, 1675 age 25 (sui), eldest son of Huang Wu [q. v.], Ch'ing general, was a native of Pring-ho, Fukien. When his father died (1674) Huang Fang-tu outwardly accepted Kêng Ching-chung's [q. v.] invitation to join in the rebellion but secretly recruited 6,000 volunteers to defend Chang-chou, and at the same time reported his decision to Peking.",
          "source": "eccp-3640009",
